Subject: [PATCH] wave: retain exact SID ownership through native station failures

Prepare reservation and release replies before changing firmware ownership.
Fence uncertain command results, withdraw a released SID before requesting its
replacement, and propagate release failure into interface teardown's existing
terminal fence. A failed replacement must not reuse the old peer's released SID.

--- a/wireless/driver/linux/core_config.c
+++ b/wireless/driver/linux/core_config.c
@@ -1115,35 +1115,55 @@
 {
